# The 512-byte EEPROM the published Golden Balloon 1.7.0 build wrote after
# one Adventure door and one race from a new game. Provenance, and the
# facts each byte range carries: README.md beside this file.
#
# Format: a `size` line, then `OFFSET: BYTES` rows in hex. Every byte of
# the image appears exactly once; a reader refuses gaps and overlaps.
size 512
# slot 1 (bytes 0-39): valid; the Adventure file the route created
0000: 00 50 02 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 04 04 00 00 00 00
0014: 04 03 00 36 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 04 00 00 00 00 00
# slot 2 (bytes 40-79): empty, erased to 0xFF
0028: ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
003c: ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
# slot 3 (bytes 80-119): empty, erased to 0xFF
0050: ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
0064: ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff
# settings (bytes 120-127): never written by this route
0078: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
# fastest laps (bytes 128-319): never written; no Time Trial was run
0080: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
0090: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00a0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00b0: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
